. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         *Our measure of gender support for gender equality (as measured with 
> attitudes) is the variable GEattitude. 
.         *We constructed this measure based on the agreement to two statements
>  to "Women have the same rights as men" 
.         *(constructed from plj0620) and "At home, the husband should have the
>  final say" 
.         *(constructed from plj0625), which we rescaled, reversed, and average
> d so that higher values mean 
.         *more support for gender equality on a scale that ranges from 0 to 10
> .
.         * We want to test whether the having daughters leads to a larger incr
> ease in the support of gender equality for men than for women (hypothesis 4).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with GEattitud
> e as dependent variable and the dummy variable d_daughter as independent vari
> able, a male dummy, and an interaction term of the two. The coefficient on th
> e interaction term shows by how much estimated effect differes between men an
> d women, with positive values indicating that the estimated effect of having 
> at least one daugher is stronger for men. We include additional control varia
> bles. 
. 
. reg GEattitude maledaughter d_daughter male age kid1age  germborn i.edu i.sye
> ar,cluster (hid)
note: germborn omitted because of collinearity.

